expected_issues.description:
**BUG: Potential Null Return Not Handled**

The method `getDataSource().getCatalog(activeCatalogName)` can return `null` if the catalog with the given name doesn't exist. This null value would be returned directly without any handling, which could cause `NullPointerException` in calling code expecting a non-null catalog.

**Suggested Fix:**
```java
@Nullable
@Override
public GenericCatalog getDefaultCatalog() {
    if (CommonUtils.isEmpty(activeCatalogName)) {
        return super.getDefaultCatalog();
    }
    GenericCatalog catalog = getDataSource().getCatalog(activeCatalogName);
    if (catalog == null) {
        log.debug("Catalog '" + activeCatalogName + "' not found, falling back to super implementation");
        return super.getDefaultCatalog();
    }
    return catalog;
}
```

